/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Types: Lookup
 *   Functions: applied, withLookup, notStarted, Lookup, mount, nameBox, lookupReads, statusLine, expectStatus,
 *              primaries, retitled
 *   Constants: completeOne, possiblePairing, keepsRunning, proposedHint
 * Tests
 *   - before any run the summary says so and prefills the name box with the saved Album title, which submits as a lookup of that kind
 *   - a completed run that found nothing to use suggests the name without its subtitle, describing the name field; a run that found releases does not
 *   - where lookup is not configured there is no name box and no retry
 *   - the free retry is a plain control while lookup retries, is unavailable or stopped, it retries the run, and no Luna AI control is ever among the lookup parts
 *   - conflict answers name the applied source and answer one conflict against its saved value; precision and ID-only conflicts say so
 *   - bulk answers send every open conflict, members included, in one request; one conflict has no bulk answer; answers wait while a run is active
 *   - an iTunes-only application names iTunes on its answers and flags each value it wrote as iTunes only and not checked
 *   - the label flag, and an artist mismatch only for this run's preselection, are values to check; MusicBrainz values are folded
 *   - Track Artists show a member filled from its own release track, one in conflict with its answers, and one unchanged with its reason
 *   - member conflicts alone take their answers in their own rows: one has no bulk answer, two have both, and no empty Album conflicts region shows
 *   - the expected tracklist shows each row with its members, rows without a file and members outside it; an open conflict shows the lookup rows
 *   - a tie offers the review's candidates with its own copy and applies nothing, so no member rows, tracklist or identity rows show
 *   - the summary polls while a run is active, and a read whose value revision or revision is newer than the detail's reads the review detail again, its first read included
 *   - a refused answer or an edit conflict reads the summary and the identity rows again
 *   - a failed read says so and reads again on Try again
 *   - a disabled summary disables every control it shows, its identity cards dimmed, except the MusicBrainz ID toggle
 *   - an earlier run's application stays the review's: its conflicts, member rows and identity rows show while a new run waits
 *   - a value lookup could not apply reads as its own reason, Album values and track fields alike, while members keep theirs in their own rows
 *   - the review's saved tracklist shows with its rows without a file when the applied release offers none, and when nothing is applied
 *   - answered conflicts leave the conflicts and fold away once with the answer given and the source used; an answered member says the same in its row
 *   - each lookup outcome reads in the review's own words, with the retry only where lookup stopped short, and nothing applied shows no applied rows
 *   - while Luna AI runs, alone or beside the lookup, the status line names it with a sentence saying the draft can be checked meanwhile, never why the update waits
 *   - identity rows wait until the review's Album is current again, and are never read meanwhile
 *   - the summary polls while its run is active and stops once it is unmounted
 *   - a possible release whose tracks pair in more than one way leads the status, which points at the numbers proposed from the captured titles, with no fill and no primary button
 *   - the review names the cause where nothing matched: members without a duration, an Album without members, titles without positions, or a real no match
 *   - once saved numbers make a possible release pair in one way while durations are unknown, the summary says to use it and offers no fill
 *   - once saved numbers make the release match, its offer is said once, as the status, and Use this release on its card naming both editions is the only primary button
 *   - a song lookup compares the releases with the saved Album title, and a release applied for its Album values only is said to bring in its tracklist when used again
 *   - an active run says whether it is queued or which step runs, with its counts and that the draft can be checked meanwhile; its Details log holds the time since it started and that it keeps running
 *   - the polite status of a running step does not change between polls; only the elapsed time in its log moves
 *   - while a run is active, a name is looked up only after confirming that it stops that run; Cancel sends nothing
 *   - the open-answer counters lead the lookup details after the status line, then the identity rows, and the details and identity rows carry the lookup and identity anchors
 *   - an iTunes-only result checked against MusicBrainz, and an artist mismatch, keep the results open with their values to check once nothing else is open
 *   - once an applied release leaves nothing open the results fold under one disclosure, which stays open while an answer or an active run waits; the identity rows sit outside it
 *   - a release applied for its Album values only keeps the results open while its tracks pair in more than one way and the titles propose the numbers, saying after them why and what saving them does
 *   - a retrying run says when it retries in the interface language and which retry of how many, with the free retry as a plain button
 *   - while a run is active its steps follow the status, and after a completed run its record and the names searched wait behind Details, before the name box
 *   - the name box sends its prefilled Artists as none only while they are the captured names the server searches, and refills when they change
 *   - the status stays one mounted live region as the first run appears and its steps load beside it
 *   - the name box opens by itself only where the status makes it the next step, and the administrator's choice holds for the run it was made in
 *   - an open pairing panel keeps its saved state when its save's re-rank applies another release and the choice after it fails
 * @end-catalog */

import { useState } from 'react';
